  "response": "A, finding the dishes still there after B agreed to wash them understandably left you feeling taken for granted. That feeling matters, but the dishes alone do not establish that B expected you to do them or intended to devalue you. Since you have not asked what happened, B’s explanation remains unknown. You could say, “We agreed you would wash the dishes last night. Seeing them this morning, I felt taken for granted and wondered whether you expected me to handle them. What happened?” Then discuss how to follow through on shared chores and communicate when plans change."
